+Why these changes work (brief math intuition)
+
+Masking the entire loss ensures the stochastic objective you’re optimizing matches the kept subset; without it, the KL term biases the policy toward the reference on rejects — a different objective than your masked PG.
+
+Log‑space clipping keeps the trust region additive in log‑prob space; multiplicative ratio clipping is asymmetric and reacts poorly to heavy tails from sequence‑level IS.
+
+SNIS within groups reduces variance by normalizing out scale when a group contains rare, high‑weight sequences; it keeps the direction of the gradient aligned because PPO’s min() still applies to the normalized weights.
